ity shall not affect the other provisions of these terms and rules Full legal effect. \n5. You should fulfill your obligation to fill out and sign all documents and meet the requirements of {name} through these terms and rules, so that {name} can benefit from these terms and rules, protect and enforce these terms and rules, and Let it be fully effective. \n6. These terms and rules cannot establish or be regarded as the establishment of cooperation, joint venture or agency relationship between the parties. At the same time, unless expressly stated otherwise in these terms and rules, no party has the right to bind any other party in any way.\n7. {name} must not violate these terms and rules, if {name} delays or fails to perform its obligations, and the delay or failure to perform is caused by the event itself or by reasons or circumstances outside the control of {name}, {Name} shall not be liable for this. These uncontrollable reasons or circumstances include (but are not limited to) any telecommunication network failure, power outage, third-party computer hardware or software failure, fire, lightning, explosion, flood, severe weather, Industrial disputes or work stoppages, terrorist activities, and actions by governments or other authorities. In this case, the performance time should be extended, and the extended time is equivalent to the time when the performance of the obligation is delayed or cannot be performed. \n8. {name} may assign, transfer, charge, sub-authorize or deal with these terms and rules in any other way, or subcontract any rights and obligations in these terms and rules to members of the {name} group Any company.\n9. Under these terms and rules, any notice must be given in written English and can be delivered by hand, first-class mail, record delivery, registered mail, air mail, e-mail or fax to: (a ) For {name}, the relevant {name} company address listed at the beginning of these terms and rules or as shown on the website; and (b) For {name}’s notice to you, follow customer registration procedures (including Any data changes that you have notified {name}). Any notice is deemed to have been received on the basis: (a) if it is delivered by hand, at the time of delivery; (b) if it is delivered by first-class mail, record delivery, or registered mail, the second after the day of mailing 9:30 am (GMT) on the full day; (c) if it is sent by prepaid registered air mail, at 9:30 am (GMT) on the fifth full day after the day of the post; (d) if sent by e-mail , When sending; and (e) If sending by fax, when sending by the sender.\n10. The appendices, privacy policy, cookies policy, rules, any explicitly mentioned documents, any guidelines or rules posted on the website are an integral part of these terms and rules, and are the subject of these terms and rules Part is equally effective. If there is any inconsistency between the subject and these terms and the rules, appendices, privacy policy, cookies policy, rules and/or any documents explicitly mentioned therein, any guidelines or rules posted on the website, unless otherwise stated, the subject Prevail. \nI. Complaints, disputes, applicable law and jurisdiction\n1. If any claims or disputes arise from past or current transactions, please contact us. If {name} is unable to resolve the dispute, either party has the right to transfer the relevant dispute to an arbitration institution, such as Independent Gaming Arbitration Service (IBAS). In the case where all parties to the dispute have full representatives, IBAS will make a final ruling ( Unless there is an obvious error). Unless {name} does not follow the arbitration decision, any dispute over betting will not result in litigation, legal measures or the revocation of gaming licenses or permits (including any remote operator's license or personal license).",
  "about_content_privacy_policy":
      "Privacy Policy (Customer)\nThis privacy policy will describe how {name} handles the information and data you provide to us to help us maintain your relationship with {name}. \nWe will process any personal information about you provided to us or held by us in accordance with the provisions of this privacy policy. This information may be provided via the {name} website (\"Website\"), telephone or any other means. \nAccepting the privacy policy means that you understand and accept the use of your information in accordance with this privacy policy. If you do not agree to the terms of this privacy policy, please do not use the website or provide us with your personal information. \nContact us\nIf you have any concerns, or want to learn more about how we handle personal data, please contact us via {email}. \nProtect your personal data\nYour personal data is not only protected by {name}'s high quality, high investment and high standards, but also protected by law. According to the law, we must have a legitimate reason when processing your personal information, and the reason must be one of the following:\nPerform any contract between us and you\nWe have a legal obligation to this\nWhen you agree to our processing In the case of \nwhen it is in our legitimate interest\nwhen it is in the public interest\nwhen it is in your vital interest\nlegitimate interest\nwhen we process your personal data for business or commercial reasons, this Such situations are called legitimate rights.Your personal data is still protected and we cannot process it in a way that is unfair to you or your interests. \nWhen we process your personal data for legitimate rights and interests, we will inform you of the situation and our legitimate rights and interests, and provide you with a way to raise questions or objections. However, strong and legitimate reasons for processing this information may deny your right to protest. \nWhen we store your personal data\nWhen your data is stored in {name}, we will ensure that it is reasonably protected and used only for acceptable purposes. \nWe will retain your data while you are a customer of {name}. \nIf you are no longer a customer of {name}, in order to fulfill the purposes listed in this policy and fulfill the obligations stipulated by relevant laws and regulations, we will retain your data for the shortest time required. If we are unable to delete your personal data due to technical reasons, its retention period may be extended. \nWhy do we process your personal data\nIf you choose not to provide personal data, this may prevent us from fulfilling our legal and contractual obligations or provide you with the services required to manage your account. Failure to provide your personal data may result in our inability to provide products or services to you.\nInformation collection\nThe information and data we may collect, use and process about you include:\nThe information you provide to us by filling in the form on the website, or any other information you submit to us through the website or email Information\nCommunication records provided via website, email, telephone or other channels\nYour response to our surveys or customer research\nDetails of your transactions with us via website, telephone or other channels\nYou Details of the website visited, including but not limited to traffic data, location data, web logs or other communication data. \nWe will also collect personal data from publicly available sources, such as Internet searches, the British Companies Registry, and broadcast media when it is reasonable and does not harm your rights and freedoms. \nTelephone calls\nFor training and security purposes, we will record calls to and from the customer contact center, and record solutions to any questions you encounter during the use of the service. \nSocial features of our products\nIf you choose to participate in any social features provided by our products (such as chat rooms), {name} may store, record or otherwise process these data.\nCookies use\nTo learn more about how we use cookies, please review our Cookies Policy. \nPersonal information we share with others\nWe may share your personal information within {name} or with the following other agencies:\nlaw enforcement agencies, regulatory agencies and other authorities\ncredit rating agencies\n Anti-fraud agency\nIdentity verification agency\nSports management agency\nOrganization that introduces you to us\nThird parties who share your data with us at your request (or permission)\nProvide products or Necessary third parties for services\nDepending on the products you choose to use, we may need to share your personal data with third parties that provide these services. If your personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area (\"EEA\"), we need appropriate protection measures. \nWe may also disclose personal information to other companies, business partners, or company heirs in cooperation or affiliates.\nData transfer outside the EEA\nWe will transfer your personal data to areas outside of the EEA only in the following circumstances:\nYou have given explicit consent, or\nit is necessary for us to establish or fulfill your contract with us Contract; or\ncompliance with legal responsibilities or obligations\nWhen we transfer your personal data to regions outside the EEA for our organization or our business partners, we will take steps to ensure that it is subject to the same standards as in the EEA The specific basis for protection is one of the following:\nThe European Commission has determined that the country that receives your personal data provides the same level of protection as the EEA. For more information, please refer to the European Commission Ministry of Justice website. \nWe will use the contract to require the data recipient to protect your personal data to meet the same standards as in the EEA. \nThe data is transferred to the United States, and the recipient of the data has been registered with the US Privacy Shield. The framework provided by the US Privacy Shield will ensure that personal data protection reaches the level recognized by the European Union. Please visit the European Commission’s Department of Justice website for more information about the U.S. Privacy Shield. \nIn some cases, we may be forced by law to disclose your personal data to third parties, and may have limited control over the way they protect data.\nYour rights to personal data\nWe will assist you to exercise any rights to your personal data, including:\nWithdrawal of consent in any case where we request your consent, but this will not make us previously agreed by you Processing is invalid\nComplain to any relevant data protection bureau\nAccess your personal data held or processed by us\nCorrect any incorrect or outdated personal data\nDelete any personal data processed by us\nIn certain circumstances To restrict our processing of your personal data\nrequiring us to provide you or other companies you designate with certain aspects of your personal data, usually referred to as the \"right of transfer\"\nto oppose our ongoing data for our own legitimate rights Processing\nObject to a decision that is completely automated, express your views and request a review of the decision\nFor more information about these rights, please contact {email}\nChanges to the Privacy Statement\nWe This policy may be updated from time to time, please check it frequently.\nIf there are any major changes to this privacy policy, we will make reasonable efforts to notify you in advance via email, website notification or other agreed communication channels. We will notify you of the changes in advance, so that you have some time for consideration and understanding before the changes take effect. \nWe will not implement major changes to the privacy policy without your explicit consent. If you refuse to accept the changes to the privacy policy, or do not accept the changes within the specified period, we may not be able to continue to provide some or all of our products and services.",
  "about_content_cookies_policy":
      "The {name} website (this \"website\") uses cookies to provide customers with better and more personalized services. \nThis Cookies Policy will explain what cookies are, how cookies are used on the site, and how to manage the use of cookies. \nWhat is a cookie?\nCookies are small text files containing a small amount of information, which will be transmitted and stored on your computer, smart phone or other terminal device when you use the Internet. Cookies will be sent back to the original website or other websites that can recognize cookies each time the website is visited. Cookies are very useful and enable relevant websites to identify the user's device. \nFor more information about cookies, please visit example.invalid.\nUse of website cookies\nThere are several reasons for the use of cookies on the website. These include but are not limited to:\n(i)Allow users to log in to their {name} account;\n(ii)Allow users to choose login preferences;\n(iii)Monitor and collect information about transactions on the website;\n (iv) Prevention of fraud and general privacy protection. \nThe use of Cookies can generally enhance and enhance the user experience. The use of some cookies can help the operation of the website. \nplatform's website cookies use can be divided into the following categories:\nSession Management-This type of cookie can be used to ensure the use of the website, manage session information and ensure the user's website browsing. \nFunctionality-This type of cookie stores information to ensure that we remember user preferences, such as preferred language, classification type, media settings, etc. It can also help improve the user experience, such as stopping the same information from being displayed twice. \nPrevention of fraud-This type of cookie stores information to help us prevent online fraud.\nTracking-This type of cookie ensures that we store the user's website visit information, and we need to record this information to pay commissions to our partner members. \nAnalysis-This type of cookie can help us identify and count the number of customers, and check the patterns used by customers when using our website. This will help us improve the operation of the website, such as ensuring that users can easily find content, and sending relevant and more relevant advertisements and information to each user in order to monitor the effectiveness of advertisements and information. \nplatform may use third-party tracking and/or analysis cookies from time to time to help improve the website and services provided by platform to users. \n Regarding the third-party website links provided by the website, please note that these websites have their own cookies and privacy policies.If you decide to enter any linked third-party website, please read its cookies and privacy policy before visiting. \nManage Cookies\nIf you want to delete any cookies that have been stored on your computer, or want to stop those cookies that record your browsing website patterns, you can delete the existing cookies and/or change the privacy settings on your browser (this The process varies between browsers). For more information on how to do this, please visit example.invalid. You can also view information about how to do this in the \"Help\" section of your browser.\nPlease note that if you delete our Cookies or block our subsequent Cookies, you will not be able to use certain areas or features of the website. For example: if you disable \"session\" cookies in your browser, it may cause you to be unable to log in to your {name} account. \nDetailed information about {name} protecting personal privacy can be viewed in our privacy policy.",
